  "title": "stun: distinguish between draft and RFC XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS.",
  "description": "Merge request !15971 changed the name for MS_XOR_MAPPED_ADDRESS from\n\"MS-XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS\" to \"XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS\".\n\nChange it back, because there's MS_XOR_MAPPED_ADDRESS, which is the code\nassigned to XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS in draft-ietf-behave-rfc3489bis-02 (the\ndraft to which Microsoft's [MS-TURN] spec refers, and there's\nXOR_MAPPED_ADDRESS, which is the code assigned to XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS in\nRFC 5389.  This allows those two codes (which are 0x8020 and 0x0020,\nrespectively) to be distinguished.",
